findings.fix:
Judge default-ness on the painted look only:
- links must differ from the bare link in color, or in text-decoration (line or offset);
- buttons, inputs, selects, textareas and ::file-selector-button must differ in background-color or border-top-color/style/radius;
- give bare.html the site's body font so inherited typography never counts.
Then pin a sensitivity control: probe (b) run on c5e4180's site.css (a testdata copy served in place of /static/site.css) must flag the buttons and links.

dimensions_checked.result:
One finding, m3: named colour keywords get past the literal ban, which only lists forbidden spellings. The checks follow the lessons:
- #1009: no-skip.ps1 run with -File;
- #972: one top-level test per check;
- #971: single-quoted because-prose;
- #941: signal colours kept away from the danger and ok tokens;
- #1001: headless.Open only.
For CC-001 I tried variants of the new regexes. `<p/style=` gets past `\sstyle\s*=`, but CSP and html/template's attribute-name filtering bound that, and lessons #939/#1008 advise stopping at a bound. Not filed.
